          "title": "You'll want to know: дорожать",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "дорожать (dorozhát) — \"to go up in price\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Хлеб опять дорожает. Khleb opyát dorozháyet. Bread is going up in price again."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective подорожать: всё подорожало — everything has gone up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "дорожать (dorozhát) is built on дорогой \"dear, expensive\", inherited from Proto-Slavic dorgŭ \"dear\": to become dear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
