          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "инфляция (inflyátsiya) was borrowed through western languages from Latin īnflātiō \"a blowing up, a swelling\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), from īnflāre \"to blow into\": prices swell."
